    "title": "Justin Verlander draws capacity crowd despite Toledo Mud Hens loss to St. Paul - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By EMMA FINER ,\n57 minutes ago\nA capacity crowd at Fifth Third Field saw three-time Cy Young winner Justin Verlander make his second rehab start with the Toledo Mud Hens.\nThe St. Paul Saints, however, showed why they are the International League’s top home run hitting club as they launched four homers and 13 hits to beat Toledo 12-1 on Wednesday.\n“It did surprise me about them swinging the bat,” Mud Hens manager Gary Jones said. “They got some guys in their lineup that can swing the bat, so it was just one of those things tonight and we have to be ready to go tomorrow.”\nAfter pitching five scoreless innings against the Iowa Cubs eight days ago, Verlander threw 86 pitches through 5⅔ innings and allowed four solo home runs on five hits while striking out three batters.\nVerlander, still recovering from left hip inflammation, said he was just happy to come out of the game healthy.\n“I got my volume up and I threw six innings, so those are positives,” Verlander said. “Obviously, the home runs were not great, but I just kept working on a pitch that they kept hitting.”\nThis story will be updated.",
